  "question": {
    "text": "When a piece of metal is illuminated by monochromatic light of wavelength <math><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi></math>then stopping potential is <math><mn>3</mn><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>.</mo></math> When the same surface is illuminated by the light of wavelength <math><mn>2</mn><mi>λ</mi></math>, then stopping potential becomes <math><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>.</mo></math> The value of threshold wavelength for photoelectric emission will be",
